**geomean over 186 programs that ran ≥1M dispatches** (baseline `tailcall`, 13 excluded as too short): `tailcall` baseline, `repl_tailcall` +11.8%, `calls` +9.6%, `switch` -21.9%

  ...of which the 101 that lit pixels: `tailcall` baseline, `repl_tailcall` +13.4%, `calls` +12.7%, `switch` -19.5%
  ...and the 85 that did not: `tailcall` baseline, `repl_tailcall` +9.9%, `calls` +6.0%, `switch` -24.8%

**geomean over 103 programs with a benchable hot trace**: tier 0->1 2.68x, tier 1->2 1.11x, tier 2->3 1.06x, **tier 0->3 3.15x**

  ...and what it cost: build 9.8-118.0 ms, break-even 0.00M-17.64M guest ops (NOT included in any ratio above)

**shared hot traces** (same decoded ops in more than one program — one loop, not N):
- `00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00…` (6 ops) × 2: BLIQ.EXE, BLIQ.EXE
- `00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00…` (5 ops) × 2: 04-11-95.COM, 02-08-95.COM

**geomean counting each distinct trace once** (102 traces): tier 0->1 2.68x, tier 1->2 1.12x, tier 2->3 1.06x, **tier 0->3 3.16x**

  ...and what it cost: build 9.8-118.0 ms, break-even 0.00M-17.64M guest ops (NOT included in any ratio above)

outcomes: benched 103, unfoldable 59, branchy 22, padding 9, no-samples 6

- `mismatch` — the arms ran the same program and computed different state. A micro-op bug.
- `branchy` — the op list transfers control somewhere other than its own end, so tier 0 takes an edge the straight-line tiers fall through. The arms ran *different programs*; the disagreement says nothing about the tiers. Inconclusive, not a defect.

